---
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/latin-500.css';
import logo from '../../../assets/logo.svg?url';
import Install from '../components/Install.astro';
import SourceDemo from '../components/SourceDemo.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
const repo = 'https://github.com/matheus3301/kb';
const docs = `${repo}/blob/main/docs`;
const docLinks = [
  { title: 'Quickstart', detail: 'Create a base. Write a note. Find it again.', href: `${docs}/quickstart.md` },
  { title: 'CLI reference', detail: 'Commands, structured requests and errors.', href: `${docs}/cli.md` },
  { title: 'Agent setup', detail: 'Install the skill and activate a workdir policy.', href: `${docs}/agent-setup.md` },
  { title: 'Contribute', detail: 'Build locally and understand the quality gates.', href: `${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md` },
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="A local Knowledge Base for humans and AI agents. Search, read and update Markdown with the kb CLI and knowledge-base skill." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#071724" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={logo} />
    <title>KB — Your Knowledge Base. In Markdown. In your terminal.</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header container">
      <a class="brand" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} aria-label="KB — Knowledge Base home"><img src={logo} alt="" width="40" height="40" /><span>Knowledge Base</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#get-started">Get started</a><a href="#docs">Docs</a><a class="github-link" href={repo}>GitHub <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <h1 id="hero-title">Your Knowledge Base.<br /><span>In Markdown.</span><br /><span>In your terminal.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-description">Keep what you learn in files you own.<br class="desktop-break" /> Find it, read its sources, and carry it into your next agent session.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#get-started">Get started <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h12m-5-5 5 5-5 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a><a class="hero-docs" href={`${docs}/quickstart.md`}>Read the quickstart</a></div>
          <p class="hero-install"><code>brew install matheus3301/tap/kb</code><span>Local files. No account. Open source.</span></p>
        </div>
        <SourceDemo />
      </section>
      <div class="principles container" aria-label="Core principles"><p>Readable by you.</p><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><p>Usable by your agent.</p><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><p>Not locked in a chat.</p></div>
      <div class="container"><Install /></div>
      <section class="workflow-section section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <div class="container workflow-layout">
          <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="workflow-title">From “we solved this”<br />to “here’s the source.”</h2><p>A small CLI for a repeatable habit.<br class="desktop-break" /> Search first. Read the evidence. Keep the useful parts.</p><p>These commands assume an existing note. Use the linked quickstart to create an example first, or substitute your own note path and search terms.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}/quickstart.md#create-search-and-read`}>Follow the full workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
          <ol class="workflow-list">
            <li><div><h3>Find what you already know</h3><p>Lexical search across your notes, with filters when you need them.</p></div><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Search command"><code>kb search "project decisions" --limit 5</code></pre></li>
            <li><div><h3>Read the actual note</h3><p>Get the Markdown and its current revision before making a change.</p></div><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Read command"><code>kb read 03_Resources/decisions.md</code></pre></li>
            <li><div><h3>Bring the source into context</h3><p>Collect bounded excerpts with paths, lines and revisions. Your agent supplies the reasoning.</p></div><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Context command"><code>kb context "project decisions" --max-tokens 1000</code></pre></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="benefits-section section container" aria-labelledby="benefits-title">
        <div class="benefits-heading"><h2 id="benefits-title">Your knowledge.<br />Still yours.</h2><p>Keep project decisions, research references and working knowledge in the same readable format. Use your editor. Choose your agent.</p></div>
        <div class="benefit-rows">
          <article><h3>Files, not a silo</h3><p>Markdown is the source of truth. Open the same notes in any editor. No model, account or network is required to run the CLI.</p><span class="benefit-detail">.md + YAML frontmatter</span></article>
          <article><h3>Context with a source</h3><p>Retrieval returns original excerpts, not generated answers. Trace a result back to the note, line range and revision it came from.</p><span class="benefit-detail">Paths · lines · revisions</span></article>
          <article><h3>Changes you can review</h3><p>Preview edits before applying them. Revision checks reject stale writes; coordinated plans let you update related notes together.</p><span class="benefit-detail">Preview → review → apply</span></article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="docs" class="docs-section section container" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
        <div class="docs-heading"><h2 id="docs-title">Less guessing.<br />More reference.</h2><p>The documentation lives with the source.<br />Start small, then go as deep as you need.</p></div>
        <div class="docs-links">{docLinks.map((link) => <a href={link.href}><div><h3>{link.title}</h3><p>{link.detail}</p></div><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>)}</div>
        <div class="optional-mcp"><p>Prefer a protocol connection? <a href={`${docs}/mcp.md`}>Use the optional stdio MCP interface</a> with its own tool guidance; no CLI skill required.</p><a href={`${repo}/blob/main/llms.txt`}>llms.txt <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer container"><a class="brand" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}><img src={logo} alt="" width="30" height="30" /><span>Knowledge Base</span></a><p>Local knowledge. Open format.</p><nav aria-label="Footer navigation"><a href={`${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}licenses/instrument-sans.txt`}>Instrument Sans license</a><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}licenses/ibm-plex-mono.txt`}>IBM Plex Mono license</a><a href={repo}>GitHub</a></nav></footer>
  </body>
</html>
